# Byte format is part of this repository's contract, so it must not depend on
# the contributor's `core.autocrlf`. Two concrete reasons:
#
#   1. `.agents/notes/archived/**` is sealed by SHA-256 over the file's raw
#      bytes. With no attributes and `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows
#      default), a fresh clone rewrites LF to CRLF and every seal fails — the
#      first thing a new contributor sees is a red `npm run verify-notes`.
#   2. Windows recipes here are PowerShell/bash/VBS scripts whose encoding
#      matters (PowerShell 5.1 reads BOM-less files as the ANSI code page), and
#      the WCDB/registry recipes hash file content.
#
# So: text is LF, always, everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Sealed content: hashed over raw bytes, so the working tree must reproduce the
# repository bytes exactly, on every platform and whatever `core.autocrlf` says.
.agents/notes/archived/** -text

# Binary assets.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
